<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · currency</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paper money</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paper money is currency printed on paper rather than minted in metal. It was first developed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>, beginning with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiaozi">jiaozi</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> and later standardised as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huizi">huizi</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> continued its use widely, but over-issue later contributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a>.</p></div>
